title ALES206 — Lotus's reverb early/late balance, the first reflections against the diffuse wash
prompt recur loop — read REMEMBER + the 1024-round itinerary and six-season double-seat, take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, self-approve the design round, send each finished increment as its own signed round to origin and xykj61, stop at the custody gates
think ALES205 closed the tone axis whole (mono and stereo, plain darkness and full two-band shelf), so the pair is finished and a fresh reverb axis opens. ALES205's own doc named three: width (stereo spread), freeze (infinite sustain), early/late balance (first reflections vs the diffuse wash). Chose early/late balance — Lindy-first crux-first: it keeps the mono-then-stereo pairing (width is stereo-only, breaking rhythm; freeze wants new arithmetic or a unity-feedback the network refuses), and it composes cleanly from two already-proven halves with no new sample law.
think The early reflections are exactly ALES68's multi-tap (its own banner: "the discrete early-reflection pattern"); the late wash is ALES190's named-room preset. So the rung is a CROSSFADE between them at the same linear blend ALES192 proved for wet/dry. Compute early on a full COPY of the original clip (multitap_ms over a fixed per-room early bank), late in place (reverb_preset unchanged), then blend out[i] = saturate((den-num)·early[i]/den + num·late[i]/den). Published three early-tap banks (room close/quick, hall later/wider, plate dense) each within taps.max_taps, named in ms so one room sounds the same at any rate.
think Atomicity by construction: the early multi-tap writes only the copy (never the real clip), the late preset prechecks all stages before any write, and the blend is pure arithmetic that cannot fault — so BadBalance, DurationTooLong, and BadRange each leave the clip untouched. ReverbEarlyLateError = multitap_time.MultitapTimeError || reverb_preset.ReverbPresetError || BadBalance, the two halves' shared clock faults deduped by the union.
obs Witness GREEN on the first metal pass — no RED to book. Six laws on a 1024-sample impulse bench: the early edge (balance 0) equals multitap_ms over the room's published early bank byte for byte; the late edge (balance den) equals reverb_preset byte for byte; a half balance differs from both and each sample is the honest weighted average, byte for byte; the rooms differ (room/hall/plate early edges are three real reflection patterns); silence stays silence; faults forward atomic (BadBalance, DurationTooLong, BadRange, clip untouched). ALES69 multitap_time and ALES190 reverb_preset re-run GREEN beside it; TAME bans clean; width exit 0.
loom witness=ales_reverb_early_late_witness selftest=GREEN laws=6 max_clip=4096 bench_samples=1024 early_banks=3 room_taps=4 hall_taps=4 plate_taps=5 balance=1/2
